## Tangerine Standard Library — std::unicode
##
## Character properties, normalization, grapheme iteration, display
## width, and collation.
##
## DATA AUTHORITY — THE SHARED UCD TABLES: the character-property
## functions delegate to the SAME generated tables the compiler lexer
## consumes (tg_compiler/lexer.tg — the Wave-A UCD-derived tables,
## Unicode 16.0.0, DerivedCoreProperties.txt XID_Start / XID_Continue
## BMP ranges). The lexer's tables live in the bootstrap kernel closure,
## which cannot import a std data module, so the generated ranges are
## compiled into BOTH modules from the same generated output; the
## differential suite tests/unicode_shared_data_test.tg pins the two
## copies to identical behavior on EVERY BMP scalar, so a drift between
## the lexer and this module fails CI.
##
## SCOPE — what is implemented here:
##   - is_alphabetic / is_xid_start / is_xid_continue / is_alphanumeric:
##     the shared UCD BMP tables (the full XID_Start / XID_Continue
##     sets; the BMP is the supported space).
##   - is_numeric / is_digit: the ASCII class plus the UCD Nd digit
##     ranges this module carries.
##   - is_whitespace: the UCD White_Space BMP set.
##   - is_uppercase / is_lowercase: the documented BMP ranges (NOT the
##     full DerivedCoreProperties Uppercase/Lowercase tables).
##   - to_uppercase / to_lowercase / to_titlecase: the same documented
##     BMP ranges (NOT full Unicode case mapping — the special-cased
##     mappings and multi-char expansions are absent).
##   - nfc/nfd/nfkc/nfkd: the NORMALIZATION SUBSET this module
##     implements (the precomposed Latin-1/Latin Extended-A pairs and
##     the Hangul syllables listed below). The lexer's identifier_nfc
##     (tg_compiler/lexer.tg) is the COMPLETE NFC oracle; the pinning
##     suite verifies the subset agrees with it.
##   - graphemes / display_width: the SIMPLIFIED UAX#29 subset (combining
##     marks, ZWJ sequences, variation selectors; regional-indicator
##     pairs and the full break rules are NOT implemented).
##   - collate / collation_sort_key: a simple case-insensitive codepoint
##     sort key — NOT the full UCA/DUCET collation (no CLDR tailoring).

use std::core::{Option, Result, panic, Ordering}
use std::collections::{Vec}

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# §7.1.0 — THE SHARED UCD TABLES (the lexer's Wave-A generated data)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Generated data — Unicode 16.0.0 UCD (DerivedCoreProperties.txt
# XID_Start / XID_Continue BMP ranges). The SAME generated output is
# compiled into tg_compiler/lexer.tg; tests/unicode_shared_data_test.tg
# pins the copies to identical behavior on every BMP scalar.
# XID_Start BMP ranges beyond the ASCII fast path: 383 ranges
def xid_start_range(cp: Int) -> Bool
  if cp >= 0x00AA && cp <= 0x00AA then return true end
  if cp >= 0x00B5 && cp <= 0x00B5 then return true end
  if cp >= 0x00BA && cp <= 0x00BA then return true end
  if cp >= 0x00C0 && cp <= 0x00D6 then return true end
